From: qcom-vp maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] arm: add opt-in single-partition MPAM v1.0 on TCG max

Selected QSEE reads MPAM3_EL3 before feature discovery. QBox cannot define
architectural CPU registers. Add a bounded MPAM profile inside QEMU, not
an unknown-register fallback or a firmware patch. The profile has only
PARTID=PMG=0, retains security state, and has no resource controllers.
Implement enable aliases, reset values, reserved fields, EL permissions,
EL3/EL2 traps, VHE aliases, and the existing NV2 redirection machinery.
PAuth and host-backed RNDR/RNDRRS are unchanged.

Source: Arm DDI 0601 (2024-03), MPAM register descriptions.
https://developer.arm.com/documentation/ddi0601/2024-03/
Readable Arm register pages:
https://df.lth.se/~getz/ARM/SysReg/AArch64-mpam3_el3.html
https://df.lth.se/~getz/ARM/SysReg/AArch64-mpamidr_el1.html

